  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "abliterated",
    "description": "drowzeys' single-Spark stack for aday777's abliterated (ARA) Qwen3.8 27B NVFP4 checkpoint with a BF16 MTP head: eugr spark-vllm-b12x 0.27 (nightly-20260813) with the NVFP4 KV cache back-ported to GB10 (vLLM PR 49891) and the A4Q fp4 QK attention overlay. Defaults are upstream's Profile B: 1,048,576-token context by YaRN x4 (hf-overrides), NVFP4 KV, prefix caching, 4096 batched tokens, MTP 3, qwen3_xml tool parser. Upstream reports a 4.34M-token KV pool (4.14x concurrency at 1M) on one GB10; those are upstream measurements, not measured here. Notes: the abliterated build is very wordy, so clients should allow at least 20000 max_tokens; prefilling 1M tokens takes about an hour cold on one Spark; upstream's 256K Profile A is reached by lowering the context setting, but the YaRN override stays on. Licences: checkpoint Apache-2.0; drowzeys' repository carries no licence file. Not gated.",
